$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Benzyl (5-methylsulfanyl-2-nitro-phenyl) carbonate To a stirred solution
of benzyl (5-fluoro-2-nitro-phenyl) carbonate (2.91 g, 10.0 mmol) in THF
(50 mL) was added a solution of 21% sodium methanethiolate in water (5.0
mL, 11.0 mmol) and the mixture stirred at rt for 3 d. The THF was
evaporated in vacuo to a residue which was treated with water (50 mL),
extracted with ethyl acetate (2 x 50 mL), the combined organic layers
washed with brine, dried (MgSO4), filtered and evaporated in vacuo.
Benzyl (5-methylsulfanyl-2-nitro-phenyl) carbonate (3.19 g, 100%). 1H NMR
(CDCl3): 2.5 (s, 3H), 5.2 (s, 2H), 6.8 (dd, 1H), 6.9 (d, 1H), 7.1-7.3 (m,
5H) and 7.9 (dd, 1H).
