$DATUM 80-73-9
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-Bromo-3,4,5-tris(methylthio)benzene. Into a 100 ml two-neck round
bottom flask containing N,N'-dimethylethyleneurea (DMEU, anhydrous, 60.0
mL) and a magnetic stirring bar was injected
1-bromo-3,4,5-trifluorobenzene (99%, 2.5 mL, 20.7 mmol) under nitrogen
protection. Sodium thiomethoxide (95%, 4.98 g, 67.5 mmol) was then added
with stirring at room temperature (rt) for 3 hours. The reaction mixture
was cooled down to rt and then poured into water (300 mL). The white
precipitate was filtered and washed with water several times. After the
solvent was removed under vacuo, the product was obtained as a white
solid (6.09 g, 100% yield based on 1-bromo-3,4,5-trifluorobenzene). The
product thus prepared was found to be sufficiently pure (by NMR) and was
then used for the subsequent reaction without further purification. m.p.
170-172°C. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 200 MHz): δ 2.32 (s, 3H), 2.41 (s, 6H), 6.93
(s, 2H) ppm. 13C NMR (CDCl3, 50 MHz): δ 15.82, 17.34, 121.95, 124.76,
126.82, 148.95 ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
