$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM In a typical procedure, 4-methoxythiophenol (125 μL, 1.0 mmol) was added
to a stirred suspension of Wang 4-fluoro-3-nitrobenzoate resin 2 (500 mg,
0.5 mmol) and potassium carbonate (140 mg, 1.0 mmol) in dry DMF (5 mL).
The reaction mixture was maintained at 40°Cfor 16 h, filtered, washed
sequentially with DMF, CH2Cl2 and MeOH, and dried in vacuo. The resin was
subsequently taken up in 50% TFA/dry CH2Cl2 (3 mL) and mixed using an
orbital shaker for 3 h. The mixture was filtered and the residual resin
was washed with CH2Cl2. The filtrate and combined washings were
evaporated to dryness. 4p as a yellow solid (52 mg). ESI-MS (m/z): 303.8
[M-H]-, 259.8 [M-CO2-H]- 1H NMR (CDCl3, 360 MHz): δ 8.93 (1H, d, J 1.8
Hz), 7.98 (1H, dd, J 1.8, 8.6 Hz), 7.51(2H, d, 7 8.8 Hz), 7.05 (2H, d, J
8.8 Hz), 6.93 (1H, d, J 8.6 Hz), 3.90 (3H, s).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM reaction on solid support
