$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical procedure for coupling a carboxylic
acid with SPPSLRAM (0.14 μmol) SynPhase Lanterns®: a mixture of HATU (0.2
M), DIEA (0.2 M), carboxylic acid (0.2M) and deprotected Rink Amide
SynPhase Lanterns® in DMF/DCM (0.5 ml per Lantern) was stirred at 45°C
for 15 hours. The SynPhase Lanterns® were washed with DMF (3 x 5ml per
Lantern) and DCM (3 x 5 ml per Lantern). Typical procedure for coupling
reaction of thiols : a mixture of thiol (0.25M), (bpy)2NiBr2 (0.05eq),
borohydride polymer supported Amberlite® IRA400 (2.5 mmol/g) (0.5 M) and
SynPhase Lanterns® in EtOH/THF (1 ml per Lantern) was stirred at 70°C in
a reactor fitted with a polypropylene gauze to avoid contact between
SynPhase Lanterns® and resin for 15h. SynPhase Lanterns® were washed with
THF (3 x with 5 ml per Lantern), EtOH (5 ml per Lantern) and DCM (3 x 5
ml per Lantern). Information not present.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM solid-supported reaction (; RAM SynPhase polystrene lanterns used ; first
stage is attachment to resin ; solid-supported reagent ; IRA-400
borohydride resin used)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Solid-Phase Synthesis of Diaryl Sulfides: Direct Coupling of
Solid-Supported Aryl Halides with Thiols Using an Insoluble
Polymer-Supported Reagent
