$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3-Benzylsulfanyl-2-fluoro-4-formyl-benzoic Acid tert-Butyl Ester (23). To
a solution of potassium tert-butoxide (2.0 g, 17.9 mmol) in anhydrous THF
(80 mL) was added benzyl mercaptan (2.1 mL, 17.9 mmol). The reaction
mixture was stirred at rt for 5 min before being cooled to -30 °C. A
solution of 2,3-difluoro-4-formyl-benzoic acid tert-butyl ester (4.34 g,
17.9 mmol) in anhydrous THF (20 mL) was added dropwise over 15 min, and
the resultant mixture was stirred at -30 °C for 30 min before being
quenched by addition of water and extracted with ethyl acetate. The
organic layer was separated, washed with water followed by brine, dried
(Na2SO4), filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. Yield: (6.2 g, 100%);
yellow oil. 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ ppm 10.20 (1 H, d, J = 0.6 Hz), 7.84 (1 H,
ddd, J = 8.0, 6.8, 0.7 Hz), 7.59 (1 H, dd, J = 8.0, 0.9 Hz), 7.19 (3 H,
m), 7.05 (2 H, m), 4.07 (2 H, s), 1.63 (9 H, s).
