$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a stirred solution of 36 (700 mg, 4.1 mmol) in DMSO (5 mL) was added
NaOH (164 mg, 4.1 mmol), and the mixture was stirred at ambient
temperature for 30 min. To this mixture was added sodium thiomethoxide
(342 mg, 4.9 mmol), and the resulting mixture was warmed to 55-60 °C for
4 h. The reaction mixture was cooled to 0 °C and quenched with H2O (10
mL). The resulting mixture was acidified with concentrated HCl to pH 1-2.
The white precipitate was collected by filtration, washed with water, and
dried in vacuo, which was used in the next step without further
purification. 3-fluoro-2-methyl-4-(thiomethyl)benzoic acid (879 mg,
quantitative). MS (EI): m/z for C9H9FO2S, found 199.0 (MH-).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
