$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Representative Procedure. Substituted
2-chlorobenzaldehyde or 2-chlorobenzonitrile (1 mmol) was stirred, in the
presence of K2CO3 (2 mmol) and 2-mercaptoacetone (1.2 mmol) suspended in
H2O (1 mL), at 90 °C, for 2 h. At the end of the reaction (TLC), the
required product was either isolated by simple filtration of the mixture
or extracted into EtOAc. The product was dried under vacuum at 50 °C.
2-Acetyl-3-amino-5-nitrobenzo[b]thiophene (2e), yield 99%; Orange solid.
mp 290-292 °C (from MeOH); 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ = 9.23 (1 H, d, J
= 2.0 Hz, Harom), 8.28 (1 H, dd, J = 2.0, 8.8 Hz, Harom), 8.09 (1 H, d, J
= 8.8 Hz, Harom), 2.37 (3 H, s, CH3). 13C NMR (75 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ =
191.7 (Cq), 150.0 (Cq), 145.0 (Cq), 144.9 (Cq), 131.7 (Cq), 124.9 (CH),
122.9 (CH), 120.2 (CH), 107.8 (Cq), 29.2 (CH3). ESI-MS (MeCN): m/z calcd:
236 [M + H]+; found: 237. HMRS (CI): m/z [M + H]+ calcd for C10H9N2O3S:
237.0328; found: 237.0327.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM combinatorial, green chemistry
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Straightforward synthesis of 2-acetyl-substituted benzo[b]thiophenes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Debray, Julien; Lemaire, Marc; Popowycz, Florence
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (2013), 24(1), 37-40

