$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Synthesis of Intermediate 2. A solution of 1.0
equiv of 3-mercapto-propionic acid ethyl ester in 30 mL of THF was added
dropwise to a magnetically stirred solution of 1.0 equiv (5.0 mmol) of
1,5-difluoro-2,4-dinitrobenzene and 1.0 equiv of diisopropylethylamine
(DIPEA) in 50 mL of THF. The reaction mixture was continuously stirred
for an additional 1 h at room temperature. After the solvent was
evaporated under reduced pressure, water was added to precipitate 2. The
desired intermediate 2 then was collected by filtration and washed
thoroughly with water. For a typical compound, for example,
3-(5-fluoro-2,4-dinitro-phenylsulfanyl)-propionic acid ethyl ester, 1.574
g of yellow powder was gained in 99% yield with an HPLC purity of >99%.
3-(5-fluoro-2,4-dinitro-phenylsulfanyl)-propionic acid ethyl ester, yield
1.574 g, 99% ESI-MS: m/z 317.1 (M - H)+.
