$DATUM N-Boc-N-methyl-N-2-(2-thiophenylphenyl)phenethylamine (39). To a solution
of 0.617 g (1.71 mmol) of 38 and 0.207 g (1.88 mmol) of thiophenol in 20
mL of toluene was added 0.329 g (3.42 mmol) of NaOt-Bu and 40 mg (0.034
mmol) of Pd(PPh3)4. The mixture was heated to reflux and monitored by TLC
for five day until none of compound 38 remained in solution. After
cooling, the solution was diluted with 30 mL of water, extracted three
times with CH2Cl2, and the combined organics dried over MgSO4. The drying
agent was removed by filtration and the solvent removed by distillation
under reduced pressure leaving a brown oil. Purification by silica gel
chromatography (20% EtOAc/petroleum ether) provided 0.585 g (99%) of pure
39 as a clear slightly yellow oil. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.41 (s,
9H), 2.79 (s, 3H), 2.99 (t, J=7 Hz, 2H), 3.42 (t, J=7 Hz, 2H), 7.15-7.33
(m, 9H). 13C NMR (100.6 MHz, CDCl3) δ 28.3, 32.6, 34.4, 49.6, 79.1,
126.3, 127.4, 128.2, 129.1, 129.4, 130.6, 133.6, 133,7, 136.5, 140.9,
155,5. Anal. Calcd. for C14H20INO2: C, 69.93; H, 7.34; N, 4.08. Found: C,
70.15; H, 7.29; N, 4.06.
