$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3,4,5-Tris(phenylthio)benzaldehyde. In a nitrogen filled glove box,
sodium phenylthiolate (6.61 g, 90%, 45.0 mmol) and a magnetic stirring
bar were loaded into a two-neck round bottom flask. The flask was then
taken out of the glove box, and DMEU (anhydrous, 50.0 mL) was transferred
via a cannula into the flask under nitrogen protection.
3,4,5-Trifluorobenzaldehyde (1.65 g, 97%, 10.0 mmol) dissolved in DMEU
(anhydrous, 30.0 mL) was purged with nitrogen for 5 min and then
transferred into the flask slowly at rt. The solution was stirred at rt
for 20 min, and the mixture changed to a red-brown solution. After 1 h,
methyl iodide (3.4 mL, 99%, 53.9 mmol) was injected slowly into the
solution which was chilled in an ice/water bath. The reaction was
complete after 5 h at rt and 1 h at 70°C. Then, the resultant light
yellow solution was poured into water (100 mL) and the aqueous suspension
was extracted with a mixture of hexane/dichloromethane (1:1, 100 mL × 3).
The organic layers were combined and washed with water (200 mL × 3) and
brine (200 mL). After being dried over anhydrous sodium sulfate for 10
min, the solvent was removed on a rotary evaporator to afford a yellow
solid. The crude product was conveniently purified by recrystallization
in hexane or by a procedure described bellow. The crude product was
dissolved in dichloromethane and silica gel was added until the
dichloromethane became colorless. The solvent was then removed in vacuo
and the resultant light yellow solid was placed into a fritted funnel
(fine pore size). The solid was then washed copiously with hexane and the
pure product was then washed out by dichloromethane. After removing the
solvent, the pure product was obtained as light yellow needles (4.27 g,
99% yield based on 3,4,5-trifluorobenzaldehyde). m.p. 116-118°C. 1H NMR
(200 MHz, CD2Cl2): δ 6.93 (s, 2H), 7.22-7.35 (m, 6H), 7.42-7.53 (m, 9H),
9.53 (s, 1H) ppm. 13C NMR (50 MHz, CD2Cl2): δ 123.89, 126.69, 127.63,
129.64, 130.00, 130.40, 131.06, 131.95, 135.11, 135.63, 137.44, 150.43,
191.23 ppm.
