$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedures for Microwave-Assisted
Preparation of 2-Mercaptobenzothiazole
4-Chloro-6-trifluoromethyl-2-mercaptobenzothiazole is an example) In a
microwave tube, potassium O-ethyl dithiocarbonate (0.35 g, 2.2 mmol) was
added to a solution of 2,6-dichloro-4-trifluoromethyl-anline 1a (0.23 g,
1 mmol) in 3mL of N,N-dimethylformamide (DMF). Then, the sealed microwave
tube was placed in a Smithsynthesizer™ and irradiated at 120°C for 15
min. The reaction mixture was cooled, diluted with 10 mL of ice water,
and acidified with 3 mL of HCl solution (1 mol/L). Solid products were
filtrated and recrystallized from CHCl3/petroleum ether (30-60°C) to
afford 4-chloro-6-trifluoromethyl-2-benzothiazolethione 3a.
6-Bromo-2-mercaptobenzothiazole (3j), yield 99%. Mp 260-263°C. 1H NMR
(DMS-d6): δ =13.86 (s, 1H), 7.98 (s, 1H), 7.56 (d, J= 8.8 Hz, 1H), 7.23
(d, J= 8.0 Hz, 1H). ESI-MS: m/z (MH+) = 245. Anal, calcd. for C7H4BrNS2:
