$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the palladium-catalyzed coupling of aryl bromides
and iodides with thiols: The appropriate quantity of stock solution A or
C was added to a 4 mL vial containing the aryl halide (1.00 mmol) and
sodium tert-butoxide (106 mg, 1.10 mmol) in 1.5 mL of DME. The thiol
(1.00 mmol) was then added, and the vial sealed with a cap containing a
PTFE septum. The mixture was heated at the temperature indicated in table
2 until the aryl halide was consumed, as determined by GC. Silica gel
(0.5 g) was added, and the solvents were evaporated under reduced
pressure. The crude residue was purified by column chromatography on
silica gel using hexane as eluent. Aryl sulfides were isolated in the
yields reported in Table 2. 4-Methylphenyl octyl sulfide (Table 2, entry
1). 1 100 μL of stock solution C were used, and the mixture heated at 110
°C. 99% yield. Colorless liquid. Colorless liquid. 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 7.10
(d, J = 8.1 Hz, 2H), 6.95 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 2H), 2.73 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 2H),
2.17 (s, 3H), 1.48 (quint, J = 7.4 Hz, 2H), 1.26 (quint, J = 7.4 Hz, 2H),
1.17-1.08 (m, 8H), 0.74 (t, J = 6.9 Hz, 3H). 13C NMR (CDCl3): δ 135.7,
133.1, 129.7 (2C), 129.5 (2C), 34.3, 31.7, 29.2, 29.10, 29.06, 28.7,
22.6, 20.9, 14.0.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM optimized on reaction conditions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A General and Long-Lived Catalyst for the Palladium-Catalyzed Coupling of
Aryl Halides with Thiols
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Fernandez-Rodriguez, Manuel A.; Shen, Qilong; Hartwig, John F.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2006), 128(7), 2180-2181

