$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Identification of the resting state of the catalyst in the reaction of
4-chlorotoluene with 4-methoxybenzenethiol catalyzed by a combination of
Pd(OAc)2 and CyPF-tBu. 4-chlorotoluene (13 mg, 0.10 mmol), KOtBu (13 mg,
0.11 mmol) and PMes3 (2.9 mg, internal standard) were weighed into a
vial. Dodecane (10 μL, 0.044 mmol internal standard), 0.5 mL of toluene
and a solution of Pd(OAc)2 (2.2 mg, 0.010 mmol) and CyPF-tBu (5.5 mg,
0.010 mmol) in 0.5 mL of toluene were added. The mixture was stirred at
room temperature for 1 min prior to the addition of 4-methoxybenzenethiol
(13 μL, 0.10 mmol). The mixture was transferred to an NMR tube with a
septum-lined screwcap and heated at 110°C. 31P{1H} NMR were obtained
during the course of the reaction until the conversion of the starting
material was complete. thioether, yield 99%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
