$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Catalytic Procedure for the
S-Arylation of Thiols with Aryl Iodides. The catalyst (0.05 mmol) was
dissolved in dioxane (1 mL) in an ampoule. The aryl iodide (1.2 mmol),
the thiol (1.0 mmol) and the base, LiOtBu (2 mmol), were added under a
nitrogen atmosphere. The reaction was stirred at 110 °C for 24 h in an
oil bath. The reaction mixture was allowed to cool to room temperature
and treated with ethyl acetate (15 mL) and water (5 mL). The organic and
aqueous layers were separated and the organic layer was evaporated to
dryness. The residue was purified by flash chromatography on silica gel.
4-bromophenyl phenyl sulfide 11 Following the general method, the copper
complex (0.025 mmol), 1-bromo-4- iodobenzene (1.2 mmol), thiophenol (1.0
mmol), and the base LiOtBu (2 mmol) were heated in dioxane (1 mL) at
110°C for 24 h. Chromatography: SiO2, petroleum ether. Yield: 99% (for 2)
and 99% (for 3) as colorless oil. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.46-7.41 (m,
4H), 7.39-7.30 (m, 3H), 7.26-7.21(m, 2H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Ullmann coupling, Schlenk technique used, alternatively use of Cu complex
of asymmetric ligand as catalyst gave 99% yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Dinuclear Copper(I) Complexes as Precatalysts in Ullmann and Goldberg
Coupling Reactions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
