$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Diphenyl Thioether (2a); Typical Procedure. A
flame-dried test tube with a magnetic stirring bar was charged with CuBr
(14 mg, 0.1 mmol), ligand (15 mg, 0.1 mmol), Cs2CO3 (326 mg, 1.0 mmol),
thiophenol (55 mg, 0.5 mmol), bromobenzene (118 mg, 0.75 mmol), and DMF
(1.5 mL) under argon. The mixture was stirred at 130 °C for 48 h, then
cooled to r.t. and the resulting mixture was extracted with EtOAc (3 x 25
mL). The combined organic layers were dried (Na2SO4) and concentrated
under vacuum. The residue was purified by column chromatography on silica
gel with PE as eluent. The crude product was purified over a silica gel
column using PE. p-Tolyl Phenyl Thioether (2b) as colorless oil (CAS:
3699-01-2), yield 99%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 7.28 (d, J = 8.0 Hz,
2 H), 7.25-7.14 (m, 5 H), 7.09 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 2 H), 2.30 (s, 3 H). 13C
NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 137.6, 137.3, 132.3, 131.5, 130.1, 129.9,
129.1, 126.5, 21.2. GC-MS (EI): m/z = 200 [M]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
