$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the palladium-catalyzed
coupling of aryl bromides and iodides with thiols: The appropriate
quantity of stock solution A or C was added to a 4 mL vial containing the
aryl halide (1.00 mmol) and sodium tert-butoxide (106 mg, 1.10 mmol) in
1.5 mL of DME. The thiol (1.00 mmol) was then added, and the vial sealed
with a cap containing a PTFE septum. The mixture was heated at the
temperature indicated in table 2 until the aryl halide was consumed, as
determined by GC. Silica gel (0.5 g) was added, and the solvents were
evaporated under reduced pressure. The crude residue was purified by
column chromatography on silica gel using hexane as eluent. Aryl sulfides
were isolated in the yields reported in Table 2. 4-Methylphenyl phenyl
sulfide (Table 2, entry 5). 100 μL of stock solution A were used, and the
mixture heated at 90 °C. 99% yield.
